Comment (internal/service/relational/suggestions/events.go:35):
**Low / non-blocking:** `Payload` and `Snapshot` (and `Details` above) are declared `NOT NULL`, which diverges from `risk_events` — the table the commit note says this one mirrors. There, `Payload`, `RiskSnapshot`, and `Details` are all nullable.

`datatypes.JSONMap` serializes a nil map to SQL `NULL`, so any future Phase-3/5 writer that creates an event without setting **both** `Payload` and `Snapshot` (e.g. a `run_started` event that has no suggestion snapshot yet) will hit a `NOT NULL` violation at insert time rather than storing an empty object.

If every event is genuinely required to carry a payload and snapshot, this is fine — just flagging that it's stricter than the sibling audit table and worth confirming it's intentional rather than a copy divergence. If not, consider dropping `not null` on `payload`/`snapshot` (and `details`) to match `risk_events`.
